<LanguageBlock lang="zh">
	<h2>这座网站如何生长</h2>
	<p>Botanical Systems 是 Chenxi Huang 的个人知识花园，使用 Astro 构建。页面保留内容类型、主题、成熟度、来源关系和修订时间，让“还在形成”成为一种可以看见的状态。</p>
	<p>视觉与交互原型以 Maggie Appleton 网站 V3 的开源代码为研究参考，并在此基础上重写了身份、内容结构、植物系统、双语体验与个人表达。正式公开发布前，仍会继续替换参考项目遗留的视觉资产，并按原项目许可证保留所需署名。</p>
	<h2>设计原则</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>单次只呈现一种语言，减少阅读时的切换成本。</li>
		<li>用根、芽、枝、年轮、嫁接和树冠表达知识状态，而不是把植物当作表面装饰。</li>
		<li>内容可以不完整，但来源、不确定性与修订应该清楚。</li>
		<li>AI 协助连接与培育知识，不替作者伪造确定性。</li>
	</ul>
</LanguageBlock>

<LanguageBlock lang="en">
	<h2>How this site grows</h2>
	<p>Botanical Systems is Chenxi Huang's personal knowledge garden, built with Astro. It keeps content types, topics, maturity, relationships, and revision time visible so that “still forming” becomes a legible state.</p>
	<p>The visual and interaction prototype studies Maggie Appleton's open-source V3 site as a reference. Identity, content architecture, the botanical system, bilingual experience, and personal expression have been rewritten. Before public launch, remaining reference assets will continue to be replaced and attribution required by the original license will be preserved.</p>
	<h2>Design principles</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Present one language at a time to reduce reading friction.</li>
		<li>Use roots, buds, branches, rings, grafts, and canopy as knowledge states—not surface decoration.</li>
		<li>Work may be unfinished, but provenance, uncertainty, and revision should remain clear.</li>
		<li>AI helps connect and cultivate knowledge without manufacturing certainty for the author.</li>
	</ul>
</LanguageBlock>
